Greetings,

I have been wanting to mimic a plot from ggplot in ggvis to make use of interaction capabilities of ggvis. But I am facing a problem with layer_paths while using stroke=~

This is the code I tried to use

library(ggplot2)
library(ggvis)
time = c(1,4,5,10,15, 17)
action = c('action1', 'action2', 'action1', 'action2', 'action3', 'action4')
dataf = data.frame(time, action)
ggplot(dataf, aes(time, y=1)) + geom_path(aes(group=1, color=action), size=2) + geom_point(aes(col=action), size=8)

dataf %>% ggvis(x=~time, y:=1) %>% layer_paths(stroke=~action, strokeWidth:=2) %>% layer_points(fill=~action, size:=150)

But ggvis behavior of layer_paths is quite different from ggplots behavior from geom_paths regarding line coloring. As you can see from the following two graphs, ggplot changes color lines as expected with geom_paths, but layer_paths stick with the first color only.

Is this intended? Am I missing something?

